22547
ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 22547, Dec. 27, 2010>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Articles 4(2) and 6(1)4, subparagraph 1 of Article 23, and subparagraph 2 of Article 30 shall enter into force on January 1, 2011, and the amended provisions of Articles 8 through 11, Article 13, Articles 17 through 19, Articles 22, 24, 26, 32, and 34 shall enter into force on December 31, 2011.
Article 2 (Applicability to minimum length of service required for promotion)
The amended provisions of the proviso of Article 5(2)1 shall begin to apply to persons who are ordered to take a leave of absence order under Article 71(2)4 of the State Public Officials Act and Article 63(2)4 of the Local Public Officials Act after this Decree enters into force.
Article 3 (Special cases concerning education and training ratings)
(1) Education and training ratings for basic training by rank and newly appointed personnel training received before December 31, 2011 shall be rated as command competency training for fire captains and local fire captains or higher, and as specialized training for fire lieutenants and local fire lieutenants or lower.
(2) In applying Article 6(1), a person who has completed basic training by rank before December 31, 2011 shall be deemed to have completed command competency training.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning minimum length of service required for promotion)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 5(4), the previous provisions shall apply to the calculation of the minimum length of service required for promotion of a person who served as a public official under other statutes or regulations before this Decree enters into force and was appointed as a firefighting official.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning additional points)
If additional points obtained by a firefighting official before this Decree enters into force are abolished or reduced under the amended provisions of Article 11(1), such additional points shall be credited under the previous provisions.

