ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 26232, May 6, 2015>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Articles 10(2), 11(1), 22, and the Appendix shall enter into force on June 30, 2016.
Article 2 (Applicability to inclusion of leave periods for childcare leave in minimum length of service required for promotion)
The amended provisions of Article 5(2)1d shall apply also to the period of leave of a firefighting official who took leave for pregnancy, childbirth, or child rearing before this Decree enters into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to education and training ratings)
The amended provisions of Article 10(2)2 and 3 shall also apply where education and training ratings for the period from January 1, 2016 to June 30, 2016 are assigned after June 30, 2016.
Article 4 (Applicability to preparation of promotion eligibility lists for firefighting officials of the rank of deputy fire chief and local deputy fire chief or lower)
(1) The amended provisions of Article 11(1) shall also apply where promotion eligibility lists or integrated promotion eligibility lists are prepared after June 30, 2016 by taking into account performance rating scores and education and training rating scores prior to January 1, 2016. In such cases, the performance rating scores and education and training rating scores prior to January 1, 2016 shall be reflected by converting the previous full marks for each rating set forth in column 1 of the following table into the corresponding full marks set forth in column 2 and calculating the corresponding scores.
(2) Promotion eligibility lists or integrated promotion eligibility lists prepared under the previous provisions before this Decree enters into force shall remain effective until promotion eligibility lists or integrated promotion eligibility lists prepared under the amended provisions of Article 11(1) as of July 1, 2016 are prepared.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning persons subject to promotion review based on the number of persons to be appointed through promotion)
If persons subject to promotion review are determined based on a promotion eligibility list or an integrated promotion eligibility list prepared before June 30, 2016, the previous provisions shall apply, notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 22 and the Appendix.

